+3. [x] **`ta-context-opt` crate.** Traits `InputOptimizer`, `ContextOptimizer`, `OutputOptimizer`; a registry selected per slot in config; a `none` implementation; and a metrics record `{bytes_in, bytes_out, est_tokens_in, est_tokens_out, ms, lossless, original_ref}` with the full original kept on disk so any reduction is reversible. `[compression.plugin]` becomes the `proxy` kind of the input slot.
+4. [x] **Replay-able selection.** `--set optimizers.input.use=none|rtk|headroom` works through `ta golden replay`.
+5. [x] Tests and docs: slot selection, `none` baseline, metrics and original recovery, spawn flag. `docs/USAGE.md` how-to including licences recorded per optimizer.
+
+Implementation notes: the spawn flags are applied through `apply_spawn_flags` (supervisor) and `quiet` (CLI probes), and the test asserts the value that function returns, because a built `Command` does not expose its creation flags; the Windows smoke check is in the Pre-Release Checklist in `docs/USAGE.md` and has not been run (this machine is macOS). `rtk` and `headroom` are registered as out-of-process optimizers: `apply()` returns an explicit error for them, and `rtk` selection only stops the proxy (its hook is installed with RTK's own tooling), so the RTK adapter trial is S5c, not this phase. The per-goal override is read in `ta run` when it injects `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`; `optimizers.context.use` and `optimizers.output.use` are accepted but nothing consumes them yet.
